On Sunday 14 May 2006 23:42, Marc Schlensog wrote:
> you're pretty out of luck trying to get Linux working on a DEC3000.
> Although there exists a port for these kind of machines, it is pretty
> experimental. You might want to go for NetBSD or grab a hobbyist license
> of OpenVMS.

Hi Angelo,

I have one of these machines. It runs fine with NetBSD but will not run linux.
You will need to use a serial cable to talk to it until you get networking up. 
The keyboard and video are not supported by NetBSD (yet).
When using a serial cable you may need to use software flow control depending 
on your cable.

Cheers,

