On Fri May 26 2006 00:32, Bob Tracy wrote:
> Well, crud...  The "es18xx.c" patch didn't make any difference for me.
> Audio output still loops, and the machine still gets hosed (requires
> hitting the reset switch to recover after successfully interrupting
> "aplay" from the keyboard).

I see you downloaded the patch.  Any chance you could try using=20
the "linux-image-2.6.14-2-alpha-generic_2.6.14-4_alpha.deb" package (that's=
=20
what I am running) just to 100% make sure we are on same page?  I also assu=
me=20
you modprobed the "snd-es18xx" module with the "isapnp=3D0" option?  Then y=
ou=20
used aplay to drop a raw sound clip through the card?

Assuming nothing went wrong in the patching, I'm not quite sure what is wro=
ng. =20
The looping definitely does suggest that it is an interupt problem.  What I=
'm=20
guessing is happending is that the driver sets up the first 0.5s of sound a=
nd=20
then never gets (or realizes it has got) the card's interupt to tell it tha=
t=20
it is ready for the next 0.5s of sound.

In my case it was because the interupt detection code in the driver was not=
=20
managing to figure out that the interupt was for it.  Clearly something ext=
ra=20
is happening in yours.  It looks like (from the code and experimentation) m=
y=20
card (an ES1888) can configure itself to whatever interupt I choose=20
(currently 5, which is the default for the driver).  Could it be that yours=
=20
cannot?  I know that 7 was also a common pick in early ISA sound cards.

If you do a "modinfo", you see that the driver also has a "port",=20
a "mpu_port", a "fm_port", a "irq", a "dma1", and a "dma2" option.  The fac=
t=20
that you get some sound suggest to me that port and possibly a dma option i=
s=20
correct.  I take it that you can use "amixer" (or "alsamixer") to turn up t=
he=20
volume on the endlessly repeated sound bit?

What does "/etc/interupts" say?  While aplay in running on my machine I see=
=20
the IRQ (which ever I choose) incrementing relatively quickly and everythin=
g=20
else staying pretty much stable (except the clock of course)?  Before I cam=
e=20
up with my patch it used to stay fixed.

=2DT

PS:  I see there is also an "#undef REG_DEBUG" in the code.  It looks like =
if=20
you change that to a "#define REG_DEBUG" you get some extra printks.

